WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.930
<i>Suzu-chan's been busy helping 
her family during summer break,</i>

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.230
<i>but at her suggestion, 
we're all here at the beach!</i>

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.940
It's the beach!

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.950
Mira, what are you doing?

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.910
Collecting rocks.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.950
It seems she's been enjoying the 
field of geology lately, as well.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.940
She totally acts like a 
geology club member now.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.340
What's the matter, Ino-senpai?

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.430
Just thinking you two both 
look lovely and mature.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.140
I should have gone with 
a swimsuit like that, too.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.770
Would you like to wear a pareo?

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:46.320
So cute! Nice! So nice!

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.600
You look good it in, Senpai!

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:22.410
05.     Everyone's Summer Break

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:23.930
I wish Sakura-senpai and Monroe-senpai 
could have joined us, too.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.580
Summer classes sound rough.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.980
Yeah!

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.960
Mira, don't move without warning.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.770
Looks like you two have grown 
quite close to each other.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.050
Especially you, Ao.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.080
Yeah, I can talk to her like normal now.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.820
We went to a hot spring together, 
and we had a sleepover, too!

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.310
The beach is so fun!

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.260
It is.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.600
Let's swim more!

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.480
<i>Now that I think about it,</i>

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.480
Yeah!

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.050
<i>I don't think there's ever been any 
girl who was closer to Mira than me.</i>

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.320
<i>Could this be...</i>

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.350
<i>what people call "jealousy"?!</i>

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.280
I'm hungry!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.910
Why don't we have lunch now?

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.020
<i>Lunch!</i>

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.750
Ao, let's have a match!

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.120
Huh?

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.000
A best-of-three match over 
who's Mira's best friend!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Huh?!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.820
Hey, Mira...

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.430
<b>Beach House
Sea Gravel</b>

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.430
Round one!

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.390
Preparing Mira's favorite food!

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.770
How did this happen?

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.440
<i>I know Mira loves strawberries.</i>

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.900
<i>If I remember right, she likes pork cutlets.</i>

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.070
And... showdown!

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.580
I love them both!

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.540
It's hard to compare 
different genres of food.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.450
Round two!

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:53.900
A competition to see who 
can touch Mira first!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.170
Ino-senpai, please start us off!

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.990
Okay!

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.380
Though, before we start,

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.300
make sure you both keep 
a look out for rip tides.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:17.150
Beware of Rip Tides!
Don't go in the ocean 
when the waves are rough.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.210
Rip tides?

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.790
Strong currents that flow 
from the shore out to sea.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.890
If you get pulled into that current,

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.190
you'll drift farther and farther 
out to sea, so be very careful.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.010
Huh?

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.860
Mira!

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.810
Sorry about that.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.550
You girls just weren't coming, 
so I started swimming.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:30.000
I'm so glad you weren't drifting away.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.200
That was no time to be 
worrying about our match.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.850
So, getting back to business,

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:38.740
I think we should have Ino-senpai 
decide the final match. It's only fair.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:39.210
Huh?

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.250
We're still doing this?

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:46.570
Okay, why don't we have everyone ride that?

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.550
Wow, that looks fun!

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:49.650
Huh?

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:56.730
There are a few waves out here, 
so the boat might rock.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.690
Okay!

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.080
Suzu-chan, your hair!

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:02.900
Oh, sorry!

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.910
<i>She let go?!</i>

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.270
I'm falling!

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:07.870
Mira!

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:09.700
Suzu-san!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.540
That scared me!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.260
Both of you started falling together.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:26.330
I was just trying to rescue you, Mira.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.550
I was trying to rescue Suzu-san.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.100
You both ignored the match.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.000
You're so kind.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.020
If you can show that much 
concern for each other,

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.190
what's wrong with all three 
of you being best friends?

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.080
All three?

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:49.460
<i>I get it.</i>

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:55.410
<i>Did Senpai propose the boat for our 
match because she saw this coming?</i>

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:59.120
Still, this is incredible! 
You can see the strata so clearly!

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.820
I wish could show this to Sakura-senpai, too!

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:02.990
<i>I guess not.</i>

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.040
Ino-senpai's asleep.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:11.430
She's worn out from all the fun.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.230
Ao...

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.940
I'm sorry for getting you 
all wound up in my jealousy.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:29.840
Huh? Oh, you were feeling jealous?

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:30.950
Now I get it.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:34.410
I'm sorry, too.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.830
I often don't notice how others are feeling.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.870
I see.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:44.820
I'll have to tell you what I'm thinking 
more clearly from now on, then.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:48.090
Well, to put it out there,

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:53.500
I hope we can get along in many
 ways as new best friends.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.970
Oh, it's from Monroe-senpai.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.590
Huh?! Why's she in a swimsuit?!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.380
And Sakura-senpai, too?!

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.450
She says, "We finished our summer classes,

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.850
so now we're relaxing at the school pool."

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.940
Please give me those photos, 
as your best friend!

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:15.780
What is your definition of "best friend"?

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.920
Oh, Jupiter.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.790
Huh? You can see it?

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.210
Oh, you can!

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:27.630
Wow. You can tell which planet it is at a glance.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:31.340
Yeah, generally, due to its color and brightness.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:37.010
I've only learned about the stars in class,

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:40.210
but maybe I should make it
a point to learn more.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:41.350
Huh? What?

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:46.110
<b>Monthly Star Navi</b>

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:46.110
That's probably her way of showing 
affection, so you should accept it.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.820
Oh, sure.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:54.130
<i>With that, Suzu-chan's very 
fulfilling day came to an end.</i>

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.990
<i>It wasn't much longer until the 
last night of summer break.</i>

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.990
Oh, Sakura-senpai.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:03.940
I'm going to a mineral show tomorrow.
I'll send where to meet up later.
Please let me know if you can make it.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.870
Mineral show?

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.460
I wonder what that is. I'll totally go.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:08.670
<i>I'm sorry, I have other plans already.</i>

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.350
<i>What a shame. I have plans that day, too.</i>

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:13.630
<i>I'm sorry, I do, too.</i>

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.850
Huh? No one else can come?

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:20.390
Which means... I'll be alone with Sakura-senpai?

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.140
Good morning!

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.990
Good morning. You're early.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:30.480
Yeah, um, I got a little nervous when 
I realized it's just the two of us.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.280
Since you're so serious about things.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:36.830
I figured you were likely 
to get mad if I was late,

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:39.580
and you're really scary 
when you're mad, Senpai.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:43.360
What a coincidence. 
I'm pretty nervous myself.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:43.360
Ow, ow, ow!

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.040
Are you really nervous?!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.960
There are so many people.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.630
Did you notice a lot of them are women?

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:56.300
They're also selling power stones 
and materials for accessories.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.140
I see.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.640
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.600
<b>Power stone to calm a scary person</b>

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.190
Why are you peeking at my phone?!

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.680
Ow.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:11.260
What are you looking for here, Senpai?

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:15.190
I haven't settled on anything 
specific, actually.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.950
I'm mostly here for a break from my studies.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.950
It's fun enough just walking 
around and looking.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:27.010
Wow, so you're window shopping for stones!

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:29.590
Oh! It's the chisel set 
I've been looking for!

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:34.590
I'll take this, please! And this! 
Oh, and give me this too, please!

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:38.390
How pretty.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:39.600
Hi.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:42.480
Which power stone do you want?

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.080
Uh, um...

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.320
Excuse me.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.380
Could you make this a little cheaper?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.970
Okay. Just a moment, please.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:53.120
Sure!

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:58.150
You're so reliable.

00:09:58.150 --> 00:10:00.600
I'm not leaving your side at all today!

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.440
Jeez, you're just sweet-talking me.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.220
Those have rubber bands around them.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.920
Yeah, those are geodes.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:11.970
It's split!

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:14.880
The inside is made up of crystallized minerals.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:19.340
If I remember right, there's a demo corner 
where you can split geodes yourself.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:21.850
Wow, a rock splitting demo!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.060
It's the perfect chance to 
show off your iron fist!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:28.640
That compliment's actually quite rude.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:33.900
This is fun. There are stones 
as far as the eye can see!

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.530
Minerals,

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:36.990
fossils,

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.450
and meteors...

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.640
Huh? Meteors?

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.400
Senpai, Senpai! They're selling meteors!

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.340
You're too loud.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:47.600
If you found one you like, why not buy it?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.900
Right!

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:52.000
Maybe I'll get one as a souvenir for Ao.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.480
You bought a lot, huh?

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:05.930
Yeah. It was so interesting,
I couldn't help it.

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.640
This is that geode we saw before,

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.710
and the one that looks like 
it has two layers is calcite.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:14.000
There's a bismuth crystal 
with mysterious coloring,

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.480
and a pretty banded stone!

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:20.800
The banded stones you find 
all have strange patterns.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:24.530
What did you buy, Senpai?

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.320
Want to see? You want to see?!

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.450
Uh, never mind.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.460
Today was a really great breather.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.450
I interacted with lots of sparkly stones,

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.300
and enjoyed some fluffy pancakes...

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:41.240
Now you can really study 
hard when you get home!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.970
You're getting depressed!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.930
Entrance exams are tough, aren't they?

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.220
It's more like...

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:51.970
I just can't get myself into it.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.420
I know I mentioned it during summer camp,

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:57.360
but I don't have any clear goals.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.480
Your dream is to discover a star, right?

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:06.370
Yes! An asteroid, technically. Not a star.

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:10.940
If you do manage to find one, 
what will you do after that?

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.000
After that?

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:14.370
When you're an adult.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:18.590
Do you have a career or an 
occupation you're aiming for?

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.090
When you put it like that...

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.060
I have no idea.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.220
I really do envy you.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.930
Sorry for bringing up a weird topic.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.540
Kind of ruined the break, huh?

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.480
Let's get another cake.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:43.020
Doesn't it look like strata?

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:44.570
It does.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:47.620
You're starting to be more 
like us geology girls.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.900
Let's excavate!

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.620
This walnut fossil is delicious!

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:56.370
Sorry for taking up your entire day.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.190
No, I had fun!

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.730
Thank you so much!

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.090
Wh-What's this?

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:05.050
To thank you for inviting me out today.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.360
I hope we can bring everyone 
else with us next time.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.960
Well, my house is this way.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:10.470
Huh?

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:13.180
Y-Yeah, see you later.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:21.580
I forgot to thank her for 
coming with me, didn't I?

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:29.950
Silicate Mineral

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.490
<i>Topaz.</i>

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:29.950
<i>The stone that helps you find 
the path you should take, huh?</i>

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.960
<i>What a sophisticated thing to do.</i>

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:41.340
<i>Thank you for today. 
I really had a lot of fun.</i>

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:44.890
No, it doesn't seem right 
to say it to her like that.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.580
<i>I was happy you were there to listen to me.</i>

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.330
<i>I'll do my best with my studies.</i>

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.770
Uh, who would say that?

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:57.140
Oh, Sakura-senpai.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:58.700
<i>Thank you for today.</i>

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.150
<i>I'll study hard, so make sure 
to give it your best, too!</i>

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.480
<i>Growr!</i>

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:05.740
Senpai?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.950
What I Want to Be

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.670
Sensei! I want to be a train driver!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:19.500
I want to be a cake baker!

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:20.960
An astronaut!

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.170
I want to be a train driver, too.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.760
That's lovely, everyone.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.830
What about you, Mikage-chan?

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:28.620
Huh?

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.450
What do you want to be in the future?

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:37.400
I...

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:47.890
Morning!

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:49.150
Oh, morning!

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:53.500
Sakura-senpai, good morning.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.370
Oh, morning.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:00.840
Do we have a meeting today?

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:01.440
Huh?

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.250
Oh, yes. After school.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:06.950
Right.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.860
The cultural festival's coming up soon,

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:12.390
so we need to start making 
decisions on things.

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:14.130
Right.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.540
It's still so hot.

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:22.130
L-Look.

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:25.980
Wh-What?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.360
Ibe-chan?!

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:31.540
Eve!

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:33.820
I told you to call me Eve, didn't I?!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.680
She's one of my friends from class.

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:39.710
Friends?

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:41.460
Oh, it's Manaka-san!

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:43.390
Yoohoo!

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:44.420
Usami-san.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.010
Someone you know?

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.580
A classmate.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:51.760
Sorry, our Eve-senpai is such a pain.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:53.470
Reconnaissance?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.700
That's right!

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:57.980
We're a secret squad within the 
newspaper club that's taking

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:00.390
covert action to crush the 
earth sciences club's newsletter!

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:04.520
This is my first time seeing covert action!

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.270
Our Senpai is a little off,

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:11.290
but the girls of the earth sciences 
club are pretty spacey too, huh?

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.640
You said you're going to crush our newsletter?

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.890
Could you tell us what you mean by that?

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.580
I can't share too many details,

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:23.140
but our newspaper's not selling.

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:26.670
It must be because the earth sciences 
club's newsletter is right beside it,

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:28.800
and yours is interesting and full of content!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:32.880
I think we're being praised and 
reprimanded at the same time.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.720
You're such an honest girl.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.830
So you're trying to stop the production 
of the earth sciences club's newsletter?

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:39.820
Yeah!

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:43.640
I was just looking for any scandals
 that we could use as blackmail!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:47.040
You spilled everything 
in barely a few minutes.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.990
You're dumber than Mira.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:49.650
Huh?

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:52.820
Did you find any scandals?

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:56.460
I tried spying on your club 
room from several angles,

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:57.570
and I found nothing!

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:02.020
<i>I was just looking for any scandals 
that we could use as blackmail!</i>

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:03.830
Oh, my, what a shame.

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:08.460
Especially since you just shared something 
we can blackmail the newspaper club with.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.900
Huh?! When did you...

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.910
You can do whatever you want to me!

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:18.890
Well, it's not like you're causing any 
harm by peeking into the club room.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:23.020
I'm so sorry. She just loves 
making everything dramatic.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:28.020
I know! Why don't you help us think 
of an exhibit for the cultural festival?

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.260
An exhibit for...

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:31.400
...the cultural festival?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:35.150
I know! I want to create a 
model of our solar system!

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:35.990
Uh-huh!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.880
That sounds nice.

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:42.050
Last year, the geology club made a display 
board showing off their research, right?

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:43.000
Yes.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.460
Surprisingly, few people actually read it.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:50.450
I guess we need some kind of 
exhibit that draws attention.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:52.970
Something both kids and adults can enjoy.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:55.270
I know! Why don't we 
cosplay again this year?!

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:55.970
Rejected.

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:58.080
An exhibit that draws attention, huh?

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.800
You need something huge!

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:04.440
Could you bring in any giant 
rocks from the mountains?

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:07.610
Oh! You'll need an explosion too, then!

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:10.150
"Blast" would be the correct term.

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.330
I shouldn't have said anything.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:17.800
Sakura-senpai, do you think 
we could bring in some strata?

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.700
You mean a surface peel specimen?

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:24.370
I've never made one before,

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.810
and I'm not sure we have a rocky 
outcropping we could use as a specimen.

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:31.210
How about a boring survey of the campus, then?

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.160
Hmph!

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:33.960
I get it, but it's not "bowling."

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:37.340
You mean "boring" as in drilling holes, right?

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.970
<b>Boring Survey</b>

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.970
<b>Pop</b>

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:40.970
Right. You drive a pipe into the 
ground and bore out a sample.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:44.640
So if you can add an explosion 
and a huge rock to that...

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:49.350
Yes, Eve-chan-senpai. You're embarrassing yourself, 
so we should be getting back now.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:53.860
Boring does sound fun, though.

00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:56.120
Let's give it some thought.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.240
Arm Wrestling Competition

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.240
Frankfurt

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.240
Hamlet

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.240
Competitive Karuta

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.240
Haunted House

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:05.710
Excuse me.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:09.830
Inose, are you here scouting 
us out this time?!

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.330
No, it's not about that.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.170
I'm actually here because something 
strange happened this morning.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:17.380
Oh, an incident?!

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:23.090
Over summer break, someone named the koi.

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:23.090
Feynman              Dirac                Fermi            Cockcroft

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:27.100
Well, I guess that could 
make for a filler article.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:31.300
I'm surprised you noticed 
these tiny signs, though.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.200
Because I've been watching 
them since my first year here.

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:38.530
I guess some people might 
find this interesting.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:42.490
That reminds me. 
You've changed a bit, haven't you?

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:47.200
Your bangs are a bit shorter than 
they were in the first semester.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.200
I can tell because I was always watching.

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:54.870
Senpai, your heart just 
skipped a beat, didn't it?

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:56.380
Sh-Shut up!

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.710
As if! That means nothing to me!

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:58.710
Yes, yes.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.300
<b>Boring Survey</b>

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.300
<b>Planetary Model Display</b>

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.300
<b>Model Explanation Board</b>

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.300
<b>Fossil Appraisal</b>

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.300
<b>Fusulinid Stone 
Polishing Experience</b>

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.300
I kind of expected it,

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:07.200
but really trying to conduct a boring survey 
would be costly in both money and labor.

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:13.820
It says, "The harvested boring cores 
are kept under school custody."

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:16.560
<b>Staff Room</b>

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:20.270
Looks like the school only has paper records.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:21.810
I see.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:25.790
This is cute. It's like masking tape.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:29.450
<b>Soil Boring Log</b>

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:29.450
Yeah, this is how you illustrate 
the results of a boring survey.

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:32.970
Araya-sensei, do we have agar?

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:34.540
We do.

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.100
That's so cool!

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.190
It's a mock boring survey.

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:45.310
I know!

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:47.260
Why don't we serve this as a café?

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.260
<b>Agar</b>

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.260
<b>Boring Agar</b>

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.260
<b>Strawberry 
Milk</b>

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.260
<b>Banana
 Milk</b>

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.260
<b>Milk 
Coffee</b>

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.260
<b>Agar!!</b>

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.000
A café?

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:52.800
We could make other sweets and drinks 
with earth science themes.

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:56.640
A café where you can enjoy earth sciences 
along with tea and sweets...

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:57.480
A geocafé!

00:20:57.790 --> 00:20:59.320
That might be nice!

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.230
It's settled, then.

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:04.900
Ao! Let's come up with some ideas for 
sweets and talk to Suzu-chan about them!

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:05.690
Yeah.

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:08.990
Then the geology group's exhibit 
for the café will be...

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.580
Actually boring into the campus?

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:15.710
We can't do that. It's not realistic.

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:20.170
We can't ask other businesses to 
help with the cultural festival.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.610
Hey, Sakurai.

00:21:24.870 --> 00:21:26.370
If you're interested in it,

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:29.220
why not just organize what data 
and findings you can dig up?

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:33.920
But without the real thing, it won't 
be a centerpiece for the exhibit,

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.030
and it'll just look haphazard.

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:37.850
And that's fine.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:43.190
It'd be a waste to just decide it's 
impossible and completely scrap it all, right?

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:50.870
At the very least, I want to learn what 
you researched and what you thought of it.

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:53.460
I want to know, too.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:54.250
Yeah.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:03.740
<i>And so our earth sciences club begins 
preparing for the cultural festival!</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.060
06.
Hoshizaki Festival!

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.430
Next time, "Hoshizaki Festival!"
